    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1.INTAKE & NORMALIZATION\n\nCollect the automation request and convert the form data into a consistent structure."
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -144,
        -272
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "fb32adfa-ab97-4144-8a15-89b7ae926b97",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are evaluating a business process request using relevant internal company knowledge.\n\nYour task is to produce a concise, operational recommendation based only on:\n1. the submitted business request, and\n2. the retrieved internal knowledge provided below.\n\nDo not invent company facts, policies, tools, previous projects, data sources, technical implementation details, timelines, or metrics that are not explicitly supported by the retrieved internal knowledge.\n\nIf the internal knowledge does not specify how the solution should be implemented, keep the implementation approach high-level and describe only the next sensible step.\n\nKeep the response concise.\nEach text field should be no more than 1–2 short sentences.\nDo not provide a long analysis.\nDo not use markdown.\nDo not add extra fields.\n\nBusiness request:\n\nTitle:\n{{ $json.request.title }}\n\nDescription:\n{{ $json.request.description }}\n\nDepartment:\n{{ $json.request.department }}\n\nApproved Jira label policy:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.jira_label_policy) }}\n\nRelevant internal knowledge:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.retrieved_knowledge) }}\n\nEvaluate the request and determine:\n\n- recommendation: what the company should do next\n- implementation_approach: a short, high-level practical approach supported by the retrieved knowledge\n- risk_level: Low, Medium, or High\n- needs_human_review: true or false\n- human_review_reason: why human review is or is not required\n- jira_labels: choose up to 3 appropriate Jira labels using only values from the approved Jira label policy\n- referenced_documents: the titles of the internal documents that materially influenced the recommendation\n\nHuman review should normally be required when one or more of the following apply:\n- the automation directly affects customers\n- the risk level is significant\n- internal guidelines require approval or oversight\n- the proposed action is ambiguous, sensitive, or difficult to reverse\n- AI decisions could cause meaningful operational errors\n\nIf none of these conditions apply and the retrieved knowledge supports safe automated handling, needs_human_review may be false.\n\nIf the retrieved knowledge is insufficient to support a specific implementation detail, do not guess. Keep the recommendation general.\n\nFor jira_labels:\n- use only labels explicitly present in the approved Jira label policy\n- do not invent new labels\n- choose labels that best represent the department, type of work, and current stage\n\nReturn only the required structured output.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
